rnosine (beta-alanyl-L-histidine) at the N1 position to generate anserine, an abundant component of vertebrate skeletal muscle. Acts also on other L-histidine-containing di- and tripeptides, such as Gly-Gly-His, Gly-His, and homocarnosine (GABA-His) (PubMed:26001783)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}